From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Weegee <748975+Weegee@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 10:17:46 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 15/16] v4l2: keep the format while buffers exist, refuse short
 buffers

VIDIOC_S_FMT stored a new format at any time and from any file handle,
also while another handle streamed or after REQBUFS. The buffers keep
the size of the old format, but every stream start and every restart
from recovery or resume programs the firmware with the stored format,
so a larger format made the ISP write whole frames past the end of the
buffers through the S2 IOMMU.

S_FMT now takes vb2_queue_lock, as S_PARM does, and returns -EBUSY
while the queue has buffers (vb2_is_busy()), as uvcvideo does; an
application frees its buffers (REQBUFS 0) before it changes the format.

buf_prepare refuses a buffer smaller than a frame of the current
format.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 fthd_v4l2.c | 19 +++++++++++++++++--
 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/fthd_v4l2.c b/fthd_v4l2.c
index 220d840..c4a8e59 100644
--- a/fthd_v4l2.c
+++ b/fthd_v4l2.c
@@ -322,6 +322,10 @@ static int fthd_buffer_prepare(struct vb2_buffer *vb)
 	int i, ret;
 
 	pr_debug("%p\n", vb);
+	/* The firmware writes a whole frame of the current format */
+	if (vb2_plane_size(vb, 0) < dev_priv->fmt.fmt.sizeimage)
+		return -EINVAL;
+
 	for(i = 0; i < FTHD_BUFFERS; i++) {
 		if (dev_priv->h2t_bufs[i].state == BUF_FREE ||
 		    (dev_priv->h2t_bufs[i].state == BUF_ALLOC && dev_priv->h2t_bufs[i].vb == vb)) {
@@ -780,12 +784,22 @@ static int fthd_v4l2_ioctl_s_fmt_vid_cap(struct file *filp, void *priv,
 	if (fmt->type != V4L2_BUF_TYPE_VIDEO_CAPTURE)
 		return -EINVAL;
 
-	/* FIXME: Check if hardware is busy */
-
 	ret = fthd_v4l2_adjust_format(dev_priv, &fmt->fmt.pix);
 	if (ret)
 		return ret;
 
+	ret = mutex_lock_interruptible(&dev_priv->vb2_queue_lock);
+	if (ret)
+		return ret;
+	/*
+	 * The buffers are sized for the current format, and a stream
+	 * restart (recovery, resume) programs the firmware with it again.
+	 */
+	if (vb2_is_busy(&dev_priv->vb2_queue)) {
+		mutex_unlock(&dev_priv->vb2_queue_lock);
+		return -EBUSY;
+	}
+
 	pr_debug("%c%c%c%c\n", fmt->fmt.pix.pixelformat, fmt->fmt.pix.pixelformat >> 8,
 		 fmt->fmt.pix.pixelformat >> 16, fmt->fmt.pix.pixelformat >> 24);
 
@@ -799,6 +813,7 @@ static int fthd_v4l2_ioctl_s_fmt_vid_cap(struct file *filp, void *priv,
 		dev_priv->fmt.planes = 1;
 		break;
 	}
+	mutex_unlock(&dev_priv->vb2_queue_lock);
 
 	return 0;
 }
